THIRD-PARTY MODEL WEIGHTS

The MIT licence above covers Pixal's own source code. It does NOT cover the
machine-learning model weights Pixal can download at your request, which carry
their own licences:

  OpenCV YuNet (face detection)      BSD-3-Clause — commercial use permitted
  OpenCV SFace (face recognition)    BSD-3-Clause — commercial use permitted
  OpenCLIP                           MIT (code) / see model card for weights
  EasyOCR                            Apache-2.0

Pixal ships with the permissively-licensed defaults. If you redistribute a
build of Pixal, check the licence of every weight file you bundle with it.

The offline place-name dataset comes from GeoNames (CC BY 4.0) by way of the
`reverse_geocoder` package. Map tiles, when enabled, are served by
OpenStreetMap and its contributors (ODbL) or the tile provider you select.
